13065	{"artifactId":"LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s8","entry":{"id":"review-143c9b5f7fbb9c31cfc3a6599bde67c1","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:32:42.098Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac36, ac37 and ac38 (DEF.md:242-244) are each designed: re-approval before resubmission, the same request with no carry-over of an earlier completion, and refusal of a non-holder's revision.","evidence":"DEF.md:242-244 states ac36 (local approval again before the push to the same request), ac37 (single thread, earlier completion does not carry over) and ac38 (non-holder revision refused). The LLD covers ac36 in §2.2 and §5 (prerequisiteFailure adds a review-revision check), ac37 in §2.1 and §3.1 (same Reference, new entry, an earlier entry never edited) and ac38 in §2.6 and §2.7 (the 'revise' gate). It builds no extra feature, such as gating define, which it leaves as an open question. [files: docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/DEF.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A content write to an in-signoff artifact returns it to draft at a new revision and leaves its signoffs at the revisions they were made at.","evidence":"lifecycle.ts:163-168 handles a content change from a non-terminal status (in-signoff and changes-requested are in NON_TERMINAL, line 36) by returning `{ ...next.lifecycle, status: 'draft', revision: {number: revisionNumber, ...} }`. The doc comment at lines 151-153 says it 'leaves approval, review and signoffs at the revision numbers they were made at'. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"signed-off and signoff-changes move only the last Signoff entry, and only when it is open, so an entry of an earlier revision is never edited.","evidence":"lifecycle.ts:255-260: `const latest = lc.signoffs[lc.signoffs.length - 1]; if (latest === undefined || latest.state !== 'open') throw ...; return {...signoffs: [...lc.signoffs.slice(0, -1), moved]}`. open-signoff appends a new entry (line 252-253). [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"signoffViewOf shows only the entry at the current revision, so it cannot locate the earlier request of a revised head; openSignoff today only reuses a request for in-signoff heads.","evidence":"signoff.ts:141-147 filters `s.revision === current`. openSignoff (signoff.ts:452-463) adds a request to openRefs only when `status === 'in-signoff'`; every other head goes through prerequisiteFailure and would open a new request through openRequest (line 471). [files: src/workflow/team/signoff.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.4","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today the gate lets 'revise' through when nobody holds the unit, and prerequisiteFailure does not check the review's revision, so both need the stated changes.","evidence":"gate.ts:280: `if (holder === null && !CLAIMING.has(action)) return allowed();` CLAIMING is {author, build} (line 139), so an unassigned 'revise' is allowed today. prerequisiteFailure (signoff.ts:415-419) checks that a review exists and the reviewer's party, but not review.revision. 'approve' checks `rv.revision !== revision` only without an override (lifecycle.ts:233-235). [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts, src/workflow/team/signoff.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"readSignoffRequest is new, and readSignoffState currently relies on reviewDecision, with no timing of reviews.","evidence":"port.ts:112-113 lists only openSignoffRequest and readSignoffState(ref). github-adapter.ts:182 runs `gh pr view ... --json state,mergedAt,reviewDecision`, and line 190 maps `reviewDecision === 'CHANGES_REQUESTED'` to changes-requested. No head-branch read exists. The only branch-level lookup is openPullRequestOf (line 141), which lists by --head branch. [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing 'revise' guarded action is reused and is already hooked, and the s7 completion hook lets it continue.","evidence":"gate.ts:30 includes 'revise' in GuardedAction, and line 121 puts it in HOOKED. signoff.ts:311-313: signoffCompletionHook returns 'continue' for any action other than author or build. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts, src/workflow/team/signoff.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"assertMayAuthor covers every authoring entry, and switching to 'revise' does not lose the s7 followed-stage block, because settleBeforeAuthor still asks with 'author'.","evidence":"Callers: workflow-rpc.ts:183-184, 343 and 484-485; start.ts:61-62; plan.ts:40; step.ts:38; synthesize.ts:40 and 70. On each start path settleBeforeAuthor (author-gate.ts:67-71 → settleForAttempt with 'author') runs before assertMayAuthor. So a 'revise' that skips the hook's blockedBySignoff in teamGate keeps the followed-stage refusal. authorUnitOf (author-gate.ts:25-35) gives no unit for define, as the LLD says. [files: src/workflow/team/author-gate.ts, src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts, src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/start.ts, src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"settleSignoff can pass `since` per request from the waiting heads' last Signoff entry.","evidence":"settleSignoff (signoff.ts:583-586) loops over refs from waitingHeads and calls `port.readSignoffState({ ref })`. waitingHeads (537-546) has each head's meta, and StoredSignoff carries `at` (line 116, 128), so the last entry's `at` is available to pass. The Waiting interface (line 534) holds only artifactId and ref, so it must be extended to carry `at`. That is a local change. [files: src/workflow/team/signoff.ts]","action":"When building, extend Waiting with the entry's `at`, and pick the latest `at` per ref.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No stored shape changes: several Signoff entries can name the same request, and the SignoffRecord derivation still groups them correctly.","evidence":"The Signoff type (types.ts:134) is unchanged. signoffRecordsFromHeads (signoff.ts:169-189) groups completed entries by request.ref, dedupes on artifactId+revision and takes the latest `at` as completedAt. An earlier open entry left behind is never 'completed', so it is not counted. [files: src/workflow/team/signoff.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Re-running design.story or design.epic over an in-signoff artifact keeps the prior lifecycle (its signoffs array) through the content write, so the last Signoff entry is still there to name the earlier request.","evidence":"writeArtifact's content path (storage.ts:252-254) reconciles from `meta['lifecycle']` of the NEXT head. reconcileLifecycle (lifecycle.ts:168) spreads `next.lifecycle`, not the prior one. So the signoffs survive only if the finalized draft's meta carries the prior lifecycle. I did not find where the workflow finalizer (workflow-rpc.ts:332-347 writes `finalized.renderedJson`) copies the prior head's lifecycle. If a freshly synthesized draft carries a new lifecycle with `signoffs: []` (as decode.ts:39 and unit-head.ts:63 build), signoffsOfMeta would find no earlier entry, and a new request would be opened, against ac37. [files: src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts]","action":"Confirm, and add to the integration test, that a re-authored LLD or HLD keeps meta.lifecycle.signoffs from the prior head. If it does not, carry the prior lifecycle in the content write.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The only change to a shared contract owned elsewhere is the sc4 'revise' rule for an unassigned unit, and it is proposed as an amendment rather than redesigned in place.","evidence":"The LLD §4 names the sc4 amendment, and the gate change is confined to the 'revise' branch at gate.ts:280. TrackerPort (sc1, s1) gets only optional additions, with no new capability. Lifecycle (sc3) and SignoffRecord (sc5) types are unchanged. Claim, release, parking and issue creation are left alone. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts]","action":"File the sc4 amendment for 'revise' when nobody holds the unit before building.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Counting a request as changes-requested from 'each reviewer's latest review' that requests changes after `since` matches GitHub's own decision.","evidence":"The current adapter relies on GitHub's reviewDecision (github-adapter.ts:182,190), which ignores COMMENTED reviews: a reviewer who requests changes and then leaves a plain comment still yields CHANGES_REQUESTED. As written in §2.4 ('among each reviewer's latest review, one requests changes'), the reviewer's latest review would then be COMMENTED, and the request would read as open, so the head would stay in-signoff after a real request for changes on the new push. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"Specify that each reviewer's latest decisive review (APPROVED, CHANGES_REQUESTED or DISMISSED; COMMENTED ignored) is the one compared with `since`, and add a contract case for a later COMMENTED review.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A failed read of the earlier request and a branch mismatch are both detected, and neither falls back to opening a new request.","evidence":"openSignoff returns early on each failed PortResult (signoff.ts:437-447), and publishArtifactsBranch returns the current branch (signoff.ts:370-385), so a comparison with readSignoffRequest's branch is possible. The LLD §5 states a rejected result for both and no fallback. The no-readSignoffRequest fallback relies on openSignoffRequest reusing an open PR on the branch, which exists (github-adapter.ts:158-160). [files: src/workflow/team/signoff.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of ac36, ac37 and ac38 maps to named unit, contract or integration tests, and the s7 test worlds they extend exist.","evidence":"The §6 acceptance mapping lists tests for all three criteria. The fixtures named exist: src/workflow/team/__tests__/signoff.test.ts and signoff-e2e.test.ts, and the fake gh in src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/github-signoff.test.ts, whose readSignoffState case (lines 110-127) the new `since` contract test extends. [files: src/workflow/team/__tests__/signoff.test.ts, src/workflow/team/__tests__/signoff-e2e.test.ts, src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/github-signoff.test.ts]","action":"Add an integration case asserting that the re-authored head still carries its earlier Signoff entry (see data-compatibility).","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":1,"low":14,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-22T17:32:42.098Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
