12959	{"artifactId":"LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s8","entry":{"id":"review-e5178770ea3573af006572f4585b52d5","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:41:05.524Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac36/ac37/ac38 (DEF.md:242-244) are each designed: re-approval before push to the same request, a single thread with no carried-over completion, and refusal of a non-holder's revision.","evidence":"DEF.md:242-244 state the three criteria. The design covers ac36 through prerequisiteFailure plus the existing approval-revision check (signoff.ts:403-405). It covers ac37 by resubmitting to the request named by the last signoffs entry, and nextLifecycle 'signed-off' moves only the last entry (lifecycle.ts:255-260). It covers ac38 through the 'revise' gate in assertMayAuthor plus a claim-first refusal. Non-goals such as a new lifecycle op (a3) and a new request per revision (a4) are rejected and not built. [files: docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/DEF.md, src/workflow/team/signoff.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today prerequisiteFailure checks only that a DEF/HLD/LLD review exists and is by the other party, not that it is of the current revision; an override-approved head therefore can be submitted with a stale review.","evidence":"signoff.ts:415-419 checks lifecycleReviewOf(meta) !== undefined and reviewer !== author only. In lifecycle.ts:233-236, 'approve' checks rv.revision !== revision only when no override reason is given. [files: src/workflow/team/signoff.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today a content write loses the Signoff history: it stores the next head's lifecycle (or none), while carrying meta.tracker and meta.envelope.","evidence":"storage.ts:241-245 carries tracker (carryTracker) and envelope (carryBinding) only. When next has a lifecycle, reconcileLifecycle returns {...next.lifecycle, status:'draft', ...} (lifecycle.ts:168), so next's signoffs ([] for a fresh draft) replace the prior entries. When next has no lifecycle, storage.ts:260-266 stores none. workflow-rpc.ts:347 writes the synthesized head with writeArtifact(...,'content'). [files: src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The s7 GitHub readSignoffState decides from reviewDecision, so a lingering CHANGES_REQUESTED from an earlier push makes the request changes-requested.","evidence":"github-adapter.ts:182 runs `gh pr view --json state,mergedAt,reviewDecision`. Line 190: `if (parsed.state === 'CLOSED' || parsed.reviewDecision === 'CHANGES_REQUESTED') return 'changes-requested'`. No time is considered. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The gate already has a 'revise' guarded action that allows the holder, refuses another holder, and allows (without claiming) an unassigned unit; teamContext and readHolder are exported for the claim-first check.","evidence":"gate.ts:30 GuardedAction includes 'revise'. gate.ts:136 lists it as GUARDED. gate.ts:139 CLAIMING is only author/build, and gate.ts:280 `if (holder === null && !CLAIMING.has(action)) return allowed()`, so an unassigned unit is allowed with no claim; hence the design's extra claim-first check. teamContext (gate.ts:208) and readHolder (gate.ts:232) are exported. The hook returns 'continue' for 'revise' (signoff.ts:311-313). [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts, src/workflow/team/signoff.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"signoffsOfMeta returns every stored entry with its `at`, while signoffViewOf shows only the current revision's entry, so the earlier request must be read from signoffsOfMeta.","evidence":"signoff.ts:118-131 returns all entries with revision/request/state/at. signoffViewOf (signoff.ts:141-148) keeps only `s.revision === current`. signoffsOfMeta is module-private, which is fine because openSignoff is in the same file. [files: src/workflow/team/signoff.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"readSignoffState has a single production caller (settleSignoff) and a single implementer (GitHub adapter), so adding an optional `since` plus an optional readSignoffRequest is complete and source-compatible with the test fakes.","evidence":"Grep finds the port declaration at port.ts:113, the adapter at github-adapter.ts:178/260, and the only call at signoff.ts:586 `port.readSignoffState({ ref })`. The other hits are test fakes declared `(_r: SignoffRequestRef)`, which still type-check with an added optional parameter. [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts, src/workflow/team/signoff.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Changing assertMayAuthor covers every authoring entry, including the re-check right before the daemon writes the draft.","evidence":"author-gate.ts:38-45 is the single function. workflow-rpc.ts:343 calls assertMayAuthor(intent) immediately before writeArtifact at :347. The author-gate header says the workflow-step phases use the same function. authorUnitOf (author-gate.ts:25-35) gives no unit for define, matching the design's DEF exclusion and open question. [files: src/workflow/team/author-gate.ts, src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"openSignoff today always opens a new request for an approved (non-in-signoff) head, so the resubmission branch is a real change inside the existing openSignoff loop.","evidence":"signoff.ts:452-474: only status 'in-signoff' contributes to openRefs. An approved revised head goes through prerequisiteFailure into `unrecorded`, and with openRefs empty openRequest() opens a new request. The adapter reuses an open PR on the same branch (github-adapter.ts:158-160), which supports the design's fallback for a tracker without readSignoffRequest. [files: src/workflow/team/signoff.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"A content write that carries the prior signoffs by creating a default draft lifecycle when the next head has none behaves as today except for keeping the entries ('nothing else about the lifecycle changes').","evidence":"Once a lifecycle is synthesized, storage.ts:252-253 routes the write through reconcileLifecycleOf. When the regenerated content hashes the same as the prior head's, reconcileLifecycle calls assertLegalStatusChange(prior.status, 'draft') (lifecycle.ts:170). From 'in-signoff' or 'changes-requested' no table op reaches 'draft' (lifecycle.ts:38-52: 'review' only from draft/pending-review, 'reopen' only from completed), so it throws IllegalTransitionError. Today the same lifecycle-less write succeeds (storage.ts:260-266). So an identical re-author of an in-signoff artifact newly fails. The design states no handling for this and has no test for it. [files: src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"State the unchanged-content case. For example, when content is unchanged and the next head has no lifecycle, keep the prior lifecycle as is rather than synthesizing a draft one. Add a writeArtifact unit test for an identical rewrite of an in-signoff head.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Older records stay readable: a prior head without signoffs is written as today, and entries keep their stored shape (no field changes).","evidence":"signoffsOfMeta (signoff.ts:118-131) tolerates a missing array and a missing `at` (defaults to ''). The design carries nothing when the prior head has no entries (edge-case table) and adds no fields to Signoff (lifecycle.ts:252 shape unchanged). [files: src/workflow/team/signoff.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The writeArtifact change belongs to s4 (sc3) and is routed as an sc3 amendment rather than redesigned silently; sc4/sc5 types are unchanged.","evidence":"The HLD adjacent scope lists s4 as owning the single content-write helper (sc3). AMD-315d510cb28100e2-22.json:41 is titled 'writeArtifact content write carries meta.lifecycle.signoffs forward'. The design adds no GateOutcome kind and no hook change: the 'revise' action already exists (gate.ts:30), and the claim-first refusal uses the existing 'refused' outcome kind. [files: .insrc/artifacts/AMD-315d510cb28100e2-22.json, src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"Approve AMD-315d510cb28100e2-22 alongside the LLD.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A branch mismatch is detected by comparing the branch publishBranch returns with readSignoffRequest's branch, and 'nothing is recorded'.","evidence":"publishArtifactsBranch (signoff.ts:370-385) commits and pushes before returning the branch, so on a mismatch the commit is already pushed to the wrong branch. The design only promises that nothing is recorded, which is true. Comparing against `git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD` before publishing would avoid the stray push, but the stated detection and response are consistent with the code. [files: src/workflow/team/signoff.ts]","action":"Optionally check the current branch before publishing so a mismatch pushes nothing.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A partial recording after the push is repeatable: a repeat finds the earlier request again and records the rest without opening a second PR.","evidence":"recordOpened (signoff.ts:515-525) returns a rejected result naming the request on a failed apply. On repeat, the already-recorded heads are 'in-signoff' with an open current-revision entry (openRefs path, signoff.ts:454-457), and the not-yet-recorded heads' last entry still names the same open request. Both resolve to the same ref. [files: src/workflow/team/signoff.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion ac36, ac37 and ac38 maps to at least one unit/contract test and one integration test.","evidence":"Acceptance mapping (LLD §6): ac36 has an openSignoff unit test and the revise-flow integration test. ac37 has openSignoff, writeArtifact and settle unit tests, the readSignoffState `since` contract test and settle integration tests. ac38 has an assertMayAuthor unit test and an author-entry integration test. The fixtures (SignoffDeps world in signoff.test.ts:284, fake gh via _setTrackerExecForTests in github-signoff.test.ts) exist. [files: src/workflow/team/__tests__/signoff.test.ts, src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/github-signoff.test.ts]","action":"Add the identical-content rewrite case noted under data-compatibility.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":1,"low":14,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-22T17:41:05.524Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
