10988	{"artifactId":"LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s8","entry":{"id":"review-e050e332502f32aa6291abf4a04a7d36","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:13:40.104Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac36, ac37 and ac38 (DEF.md:242-244) are each designed: approve again before pushing (prerequisiteFailure plus the review-revision check), the same request with no carried completion (resubmission to the earlier request, entries never edited, the `since` guard), and refusing non-holders ('revise' in assertMayAuthor).","evidence":"DEF.md:242-244 states ac36/ac37/ac38. LLD §2.1, §2.2, §2.4 and §2.6 cover each one. prerequisiteFailure (signoff.ts:395-420) already checks that the approval is at the current revision. The design adds the review-revision check that is missing today.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Revising an artifact after changes are requested covers every artifact of the request (the design's edge case 'Two artifacts of one request, only one revised').","evidence":"settleSignoff applies 'signoff-changes' to every waiting head of the request (signoff.ts:593-598), so all artifacts of the request move to changes-requested. LIFECYCLE_TABLE (lifecycle.ts:38-52) has no step out of changes-requested except a content change (reconcileLifecycle → draft), withdraw or supersede. 'open-signoff' requires 'approved'. 'approve' requires 'draft'. An artifact that the holder does not need to change, or one re-authored with identical content (which the design deliberately keeps in changes-requested), therefore can never be resubmitted: openSignoff sends it to prerequisiteFailure, which rejects it as 'not approved (status changes-requested)'. The design's edge-case row covers only the case where the revision happens while the request is still in-signoff. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, src/workflow/team/signoff.ts]","action":"Design how an unchanged artifact in changes-requested returns to the request: for example a legal changes-requested→approved/draft step, or openSignoff re-recording it under the same Reference when its revision is unchanged. Alternatively, state explicitly that every artifact of a changes-requested request must be revised.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today a content write of a re-authored artifact drops meta.lifecycle (when the next head has none) or resets signoffs (when the next head carries a fresh draft), because only meta.tracker and meta.envelope are carried.","evidence":"storage.ts:239-266: `const meta = { ...next['meta'] }`. Only carryTracker and carryBinding are applied. With no next lifecycle the else-branches mint a revision and keep no lifecycle. The authoring writers (workflow-rpc.ts:347, synthesize.ts:90) write the finalized JSON as 'content'.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"An identical re-author with a synthesized draft lifecycle would throw, because in-signoff/changes-requested → draft is not a legal step.","evidence":"In reconcileLifecycle (lifecycle.ts:163-170), when the content is unchanged it calls assertLegalStatusChange(prior.status, next.status). No operation in LIFECYCLE_TABLE (lifecycle.ts:38-52) goes from in-signoff or changes-requested to draft.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"signoffViewOf shows only the entry at the head's current revision, so it cannot find the earlier request of a revised head.","evidence":"signoff.ts:141-148 keeps an entry only when `s.revision === current`.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.4","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"prerequisiteFailure checks only that a DEF/HLD/LLD review exists and is by the other party, not which revision it reviewed.","evidence":"signoff.ts:415-419 reads lifecycleReviewOf(meta) and compares reviewerPartyOf with the author. It never compares the review's revision.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reused gate parts exist with the stated shape: the 'revise' guarded action, teamContext and readHolder are exported, and 'revise' on an unassigned unit is allowed without taking a claim, so the author entry must refuse it itself.","evidence":"gate.ts:30 GuardedAction includes 'revise'. gate.ts:208 `export function teamContext` and :232 `export function readHolder`. gate.ts:139 CLAIMING = author, build. gate.ts:280 `if (holder === null && !CLAIMING.has(action)) return allowed();`. The s7 hook (signoff.ts:311-313) returns 'continue' for anything except author/build, so 'revise' is not blocked by it.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"readSignoffRequest is new (not on TrackerPort today), and the fallback relies on openSignoffRequest reusing an open pull request on the branch.","evidence":"port.ts:90-114 has only openSignoffRequest and readSignoffState. github-adapter.ts:158-160 reuses `openPullRequestOf(owner, repo, spec.branch)` before `pr create`.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Adding an optional `since` to readSignoffState and an optional readSignoffRequest affects one production caller and one implementation, and the existing test fakes stay compatible.","evidence":"The only non-test caller is signoff.ts:586 `port.readSignoffState({ ref })`. The only implementation is github-adapter.ts:178/260. The fakes in signoff.test.ts, signoff-e2e.test.ts, signoff-hook.test.ts and signoff-hold.test.ts implement readSignoffState(ref), which still satisfies a signature with an optional second parameter.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Changing the action choice inside assertMayAuthor covers every authoring entry.","evidence":"assertMayAuthor is the single function called at workflow-rpc.ts:184, 343 and 485, and at the step phases start.ts:62, plan.ts:40, step.ts:38 and synthesize.ts:40/70. authorUnitOf (author-gate.ts:25-35) gives no unit for define, as the design says.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Heads without Signoff entries, and lifecycle-carrying writes through the store, behave as today.","evidence":"The rule applies only when the prior head has a meta.lifecycle.signoffs entry and the next head has no lifecycle, or one with no signoffs. The store path (store.ts:297) always passes a lifecycle built from the prior head, so it is unaffected. Writers that re-read the head from disk (resolve.ts:139, resolve-comment.ts:251) carry their own lifecycle.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Using the last Signoff entry's `at` as `since` gives the time of the latest submission.","evidence":"'open-signoff' writes `at` at submission (lifecycle.ts:252). Note: 'signoff-changes' and 'signed-off' overwrite `at` with the settle time (lifecycle.ts:259), so §3.1's wording that an entry's `at` is the submission time is only true while the entry is open. settleSignoff reads only in-signoff heads whose last entry is open (waitingHeads, signoff.ts:537-545), so `since` is correct.","action":"Optionally reword §3.1: `at` is the submission time while the entry is open, and the settle time afterwards.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The change to the content write, owned by s4 under sc3, goes through an sc3 amendment rather than a silent redesign.","evidence":".insrc/artifacts/AMD-315d510cb28100e2-24.json targets sc3 with the same two-case rule as LLD §2.7. Its rationale cites the run of writeArtifact and lifecycle.ts:170. Note: §4 says the amendment is 'proposed in the error paths', but §5 does not name it.","action":"Name AMD-315d510cb28100e2-24 in §4 and §5, and get it approved before the build.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A tracker read failure, a branch mismatch, and a partial recording are each detectable at a stated point, and none of them opens a second request.","evidence":"publishArtifactsBranch returns the current branch (signoff.ts:375-385), so it can be compared with readSignoffRequest's branch. recordOpened (signoff.ts:515-525) already reports a partial recording with the request ref. The design returns a failed readSignoffRequest result instead of calling openRequest.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of ac36/ac37/ac38 maps to named unit, contract or integration tests, and the seams those tests rely on exist.","evidence":"The §6 acceptance mapping covers ac36, ac37 and ac38. The seams exist: _setSignoffDepsForTests (signoff.ts:231), _setTrackerExecForTests (tracker/github.ts:31), and the SignoffDeps fixtures with publishBranch in signoff.test.ts:128-144. No test covers the stuck changes-requested case raised under coverage-of-intent.","action":"Add a test for an unchanged artifact of a changes-requested request once that case is designed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":1,"low":14,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-22T18:13:40.104Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
