12501	{"artifactId":"LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s8","entry":{"id":"review-4e8f9b9ae10f9f9e67c4073ae742319a","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:20:40.463Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"ac38 (a non-holder who tries to revise an artifact in an open request is refused) is delivered by gating the design.epic / design.story authoring entries with 'revise' in assertMayAuthor, so 'Nobody but the holder can change an artifact that is in signoff'.","evidence":"Other content writers change a DEF/HLD/LLD body without any team gate. resolve-comment.ts:248-251 appends to body.openQuestions and calls writeArtifact(jsonPath, next, 'content'), reached from the 'workflow.resolveComment' IPC handler (daemon/index.ts:739-745), which has no assertMay*/teamGate call. gates.ts:209-220 appendStoryToDefine also content-writes the Define, and its comment says 'changes body.stories of a Define a signoff may cover'. Because a content change returns the head to draft (lifecycle.ts:164-168), a non-holder can still move an in-signoff artifact to draft through these paths. The design gates only the two authoring runs and does not name these writers as out of scope. [files: src/workflow/resolve-comment.ts, src/daemon/index.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts, src/workflow/team/author-gate.ts]","action":"Either gate every content write of an in-signoff or changes-requested head with 'revise' (resolveComment, appendStoryToDefine, and any other writeArtifact 'content' caller), or narrow the summary and ac38 coverage to authoring runs and list the remaining writers as an open question or a deferred item.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac36 is designed: a revised artifact must be approved again at its current revision, and its review must be of the current revision, before openSignoff accepts it.","evidence":"prerequisiteFailure (signoff.ts:395-420) already requires status approved and approval.revision === current revision. The design adds the review-revision check, and that check is needed: approve skips the review-of-revision check when an override reason is given (lifecycle.ts:231-236). [files: src/workflow/team/signoff.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today a content write whose next head has no meta.lifecycle stores no lifecycle, so a re-authored artifact in signoff loses its Signoff history.","evidence":"prepareArtifactWrite builds meta from next['meta'] only (storage.ts:239). It carries only tracker and envelope (242-245). When the next head has no lifecycle it takes the unchanged or minted-revision branches (260-266) and never restores the prior meta.lifecycle. [files: src/workflow/storage.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"An unchanged re-author whose next head carries a synthesized draft lifecycle over an in-signoff or changes-requested head throws through assertLegalStatusChange.","evidence":"reconcileLifecycle calls assertLegalStatusChange(prior.status, next.status) when the content is unchanged (lifecycle.ts:170). In LIFECYCLE_TABLE the only steps that land on 'draft' are review (from draft or pending-review) and reopen (from completed) (lines 38-52), so a step from in-signoff or changes-requested to draft throws IllegalTransitionError. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"signoffViewOf shows only the entry at the head's current revision, and signed-off / signoff-changes move only the last entry, and only when it is open.","evidence":"signoff.ts:141-148 matches s.revision === current. lifecycle.ts:255-260 takes lc.signoffs[length-1], requires state 'open' and replaces only that entry. That entry's `at` is overwritten at settle time, but the waiting heads settleSignoff reads are in-signoff with an open last entry, whose `at` is the submission time, so using that `at` as `since` is sound. [files: src/workflow/team/signoff.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.4","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The GitHub readSignoffState today decides changes-requested from reviewDecision, not from individual reviews.","evidence":"github-adapter.ts:182 runs `gh pr view --json state,mergedAt,reviewDecision`, and line 190 checks state CLOSED or reviewDecision === 'CHANGES_REQUESTED'. The design's switch to the reviews list (author, state, submittedAt) is a real change, and a lingering CHANGES_REQUESTED decision is indeed not time-bounded today. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The 'revise' guarded action exists, never takes a claim, and is allowed for an unassigned unit; teamContext and readHolder are exported for the claim-first check.","evidence":"GuardedAction includes 'revise' (gate.ts:30), and it is in GUARDED and HOOKED (121, 136) but not in CLAIMING (139). teamGate returns allowed() when holder === null and the action is not claiming (280). teamContext (208) and readHolder (232) are both exported. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"readSignoffRequest is new (not on TrackerPort today), and openSignoffRequest already reuses an open pull request on the branch.","evidence":"TrackerPort (port.ts:90-114) has openSignoffRequest and readSignoffState(ref) only. openSignoffRequest calls openPullRequestOf before pr create (github-adapter.ts:158-160). [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Changing assertMayAuthor covers every authoring entry, and changing writeArtifact covers every authoring write (the call-site list names only workflow-rpc.ts).","evidence":"assertMayAuthor is called at workflow-rpc.ts:184/343/485 and in workflow-step start.ts:62, plan.ts:40, step.ts:38 and synthesize.ts:40/70. The step-path synthesize also writes the draft through writeArtifact 'content'. Because both changes sit inside the shared functions, every site is covered, even though inventory 3.2 lists only workflow-rpc.ts. [files: src/workflow/team/author-gate.ts, src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts, src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts]","action":"Optionally add synthesize.ts to the 3.2 call-site list for completeness.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"openSignoff today routes an in-signoff head by signoffViewOf and every other head through prerequisiteFailure, so a changes-requested head is already refused as not approved and needs only the new hint.","evidence":"signoff.ts:452-462: status 'in-signoff' goes through signoffViewOf, and every other head goes through prerequisiteFailure, which rejects a status other than approved (396-397). The new earlier-request lookup must read signoffsOfMeta for heads that are approved at a new revision, which is what the design says. [files: src/workflow/team/signoff.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Older heads with no Signoff entries, or with entries missing `at`, are handled, and no stored shape changes.","evidence":"signoffsOfMeta tolerates a missing or non-array signoffs and defaults `at` to '' (signoff.ts:119-131). The design writes a prior head with no Signoff entry exactly as today, and it adds only optional port members, so no migration is needed. [files: src/workflow/team/signoff.ts, src/workflow/storage.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The content-write change to writeArtifact (owned by s4 under sc3) is raised as an sc3 amendment, not silently redesigned, and the lifecycle table (common artifact model) is left unchanged.","evidence":"Section 4 states that the sc3 amendment is proposed and that the helper belongs to s4. Alternative a3, which would have changed LIFECYCLE_TABLE, is rejected for that reason. The table at lifecycle.ts:38-52 needs no change for a1. [files: src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Asking the gate with 'revise' instead of 'author' for a re-author of an in-signoff or changes-requested LLD or HLD keeps every refusal 'author' gave, apart from the claim-taking.","evidence":"signoffCompletionHook returns 'continue' for every action other than 'author' and 'build' (signoff.ts:311-313), so with 'revise' the blockedBySignoff check on the followed upstream stage is skipped. Example: an HLD returned to draft or changes-requested after the LLD was submitted. Under 'author' a design.story run would be refused until the HLD is signed off; under 'revise' it is allowed. The design does not state this change or how it is handled. [files: src/workflow/team/signoff.ts, src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"State whether the upstream signoff block must still apply to a revise. If it must, have assertMayAuthor also consult blockedBySignoff(…, 'author', workflow), or make the hook treat 'revise' like 'author' for the followed stage. Add a test for it.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A failed read of the earlier request never falls back to opening a new request, and a tracker without readSignoffRequest falls back to s7 behaviour, which reuses an open pull request on the branch.","evidence":"The design's error table states both. The fallback is backed by openSignoffRequest's openPullRequestOf reuse (github-adapter.ts:158-160) and by publishBranch returning the current branch (signoff.ts:370-385), which the branch-mismatch check compares against. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts, src/workflow/team/signoff.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion ac36, ac37 and ac38 maps to at least one unit or contract test plus an integration test.","evidence":"The acceptance mapping lists unit and integration tests for ac36 and ac38, and unit, contract and integration tests for ac37. These include the stale-decision, signoff-history carry and unchanged re-author cases. The ac38 tests cover only the authoring entry, which matches the coverage gap reported under coverage-of-intent.","action":"When the ac38 coverage is widened, add tests for the extra writers (resolveComment, appendStoryToDefine).","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":2,"low":13,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-22T18:20:40.463Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
