11337	{"artifactId":"LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s8","entry":{"id":"review-3f736d448940185faa9fa439537b69bf","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:28:52.105Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac36 and ac37 (DEF.md:242-243) are designed: a revision must be approved again before it is pushed to the same request, the request stays the single thread, and an earlier completion does not carry over","evidence":"DEF.md:242 ac36 'local approval must be run again before the revised artifact is pushed to the same request'; ac37 'still the single review thread and an earlier completion does not carry over'. The design reuses the request named by the last Signoff entry (2.1) and relies on lifecycle.ts:255-262, where signed-off/signoff-changes move only the last entry and only when it is open, so a completion of revision n cannot cover the new entry appended by open-signoff (lifecycle.ts:250-253). [files: docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/DEF.md, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac38 (a non-holder's revision of an artifact in an open request is refused) is designed for the authoring runs, and the remaining writers are stated as an open question","evidence":"DEF.md:244 ac38. The design gates design.epic/design.story through assertMayAuthor with 'revise' and names the ungated writers (resolve-comment.ts:251 and gates.ts:220 both call writeArtifact(...,'content')) as open question 3. That is a stated, scoped gap, not a missing design. Note that review/resolve.ts:139 ('apply' writes 'content') is another such writer. The design does not list it, but it is covered by the s5 review-fix decision. [files: src/workflow/resolve-comment.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts, src/workflow/review/resolve.ts]","action":"Consider naming src/workflow/review/resolve.ts:139 in open question 3 for completeness.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A content write today drops the prior lifecycle when the authored head carries none, so a re-authored artifact loses its Signoff history","evidence":"storage.ts:251-266: lifecycle reconciliation runs only `if (isRecord(meta['lifecycle']))`. Otherwise meta is next['meta'] with only tracker/envelope carried (carryTracker, carryBinding at 242-245). finalizeArtifact in orchestrator.ts never sets lifecycle (no 'lifecycle' match), so the authoring write at workflow-rpc.ts:347 and synthesize.ts:90 stores no lifecycle. [files: src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/orchestrator.ts, src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"prerequisiteFailure today checks that a review exists and is by the other party, but not that it is of the current revision; openSignoff takes the earlier request only from signoffViewOf (current revision)","evidence":"signoff.ts:415-419 checks only `review === undefined` and `reviewer === author`. signoff.ts:145 signoffViewOf filters `s.revision === current`. openSignoff:454-457 reads openRefs only for status 'in-signoff' via signoffViewOf. [files: src/workflow/team/signoff.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"readSignoffState today reads reviewDecision and treats a closed unmerged PR as changes-requested, so a stale CHANGES_REQUESTED decision would cancel a resubmission","evidence":"github-adapter.ts:182 `--json state,mergedAt,reviewDecision`; :190 `if (parsed.state === 'CLOSED' || parsed.reviewDecision === 'CHANGES_REQUESTED') return 'changes-requested'`. settleSignoff:586 calls port.readSignoffState({ ref }) with no time. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts, src/workflow/team/signoff.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.4","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"An identical re-author with a synthesized draft lifecycle would throw, because the lifecycle table has no step from in-signoff or changes-requested to draft except a content change","evidence":"lifecycle.ts:38-52: no operation goes from in-signoff/changes-requested to 'draft'. reconcileLifecycle:170 calls assertLegalStatusChange(prior, next) when the content is unchanged. storage.ts:192 synthesizes a draft lifecycle for a head with none. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, src/workflow/storage.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The 'revise' guarded action exists; the gate does not claim on it; the hook returns continue for it; teamContext and readHolder are exported for the claim-first refusal","evidence":"gate.ts:30 GuardedAction includes 'revise'. :139 CLAIMING is only author/build, and :280 says `if (holder === null && !CLAIMING.has(action)) return allowed()`, so an unassigned unit is allowed without a claim, which is why the design adds its own read. gate.ts:208 `export function teamContext` and :232 `export function readHolder`. signoff.ts:312 `if (action !== 'author' && action !== 'build') return 'continue'`. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts, src/workflow/team/signoff.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"readSignoffRequest is new on the port; openSignoffRequest already reuses an open PR on the branch","evidence":"port.ts:113 has only readSignoffState(ref). No readSignoffRequest exists anywhere in src. github-adapter.ts:158-160 openPullRequestOf(owner, repo, spec.branch) is reused when it exists. [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"assertMayAuthor is the one function every authoring entry calls, so putting the revise choice inside it covers every turn of the design.epic and design.story runs; settleBeforeAuthor runs before it at the entries","evidence":"assertMayAuthor is called at start.ts:62, plan.ts:40, step.ts:38, synthesize.ts:40,70 and workflow-rpc.ts:184,343,485. settleBeforeAuthor is awaited before it at start.ts:61 and workflow-rpc.ts:183,484. authorUnitOf (author-gate.ts:25-35) gives define no unit, which matches the design. [files: src/workflow/team/author-gate.ts, src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/start.ts, src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The branch check (publishBranch result against readSignoffRequest's branch) leaves nothing recorded on a mismatch","evidence":"In the current openRequest (signoff.ts:502) publishBranch commits and pushes before any request call, so a mismatch found afterwards leaves a pushed commit on the current branch but no lifecycle record. The design's claim is only 'nothing is recorded', and that is true. [files: src/workflow/team/signoff.ts]","action":"Consider stating in 5 that the files may already be pushed to the current branch when the mismatch is found, or read the branch before publishing.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Signoff entries need no shape change: an entry's `at` is the open time while it is the open last entry, so it can serve as `since`; older records without the new behaviour read as before","evidence":"lifecycle.ts:252 open-signoff sets `at` on a new entry. :259 signed-off/signoff-changes overwrite `at` only when the entry is moved off 'open'. signoffsOfMeta (signoff.ts:120-130) tolerates a missing `at` (''). settle reads `since` only from waiting heads (status in-signoff, last entry open; signoff.ts:540-542), so the value is the submission time. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, src/workflow/team/signoff.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The writeArtifact change lies in s4's sc3 helper and is raised as an amendment; the lifecycle table (common model) and the gate's outcomes (sc4) are not redesigned","evidence":"The design leaves LIFECYCLE_TABLE (lifecycle.ts:38-52) untouched, defers the changes-requested to approved rejoin as open question 2, and uses the existing 'revise' action and exported gate functions without changing GateOutcome. The storage.ts change is stated in section 4 as an sc3 amendment owned by s4. [files: src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A changes-requested head that was not revised is detectable and refused before anything is pushed or recorded","evidence":"openSignoff (signoff.ts:452-463) runs prerequisiteFailure for every non-in-signoff head before openRequest/recordOpened. prerequisiteFailure:396 already refuses any status other than 'approved', so a changes-requested head is rejected before publishBranch. The design adds only the clearer message. [files: src/workflow/team/signoff.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of ac36, ac37 and ac38 maps to unit, contract or integration tests that the existing seams can run (SignoffDeps, the fake gh, temp files for writeArtifact)","evidence":"Section 6's acceptance mapping lists tests for ac36, ac37 and ac38. The seams exist: _setSignoffDepsForTests (signoff.ts:231), the SignoffDeps fields readHead/loadTracker/publishBranch/lifecycleFor (signoff.ts:209-220), and writeArtifact on a path (storage.ts:175). The smoke test is explicitly builder-reported. [files: src/workflow/team/signoff.ts, src/workflow/storage.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":14,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-22T18:28:52.105Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
